{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1028"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c086): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c086.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1028"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge belief/philosophy","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-belief__philosophy.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",702],["+","Karl Marx began in a small city and ended in a metropolis. He was born on 5 May 1818 in Trier, then part of Prussia's Rhine Province, the son of a lawyer; his birth certificate was issued by the town's deputy mayor Emmerich Grach – an ancestor of the German television presenter Günther Jauch, a detail that turns up regularly in quiz shows. After studies in Bonn and Berlin and years of exile in Paris and Brussels, Marx settled in London in 1849 and stayed there for the rest of his life, writing “Das Kapital” in the Reading Room of the British Museum; he died in London in 1883 and lies in Highgate Cemetery.\n\n"],["=",309],["+","\n| Karl Marx | 1818, Trier | London | 1883 |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",672],["+","Karl Marx begann in einer kleinen Stadt und endete in einer Metropole. Er wurde am 5. Mai 1818 in Trier, damals Teil der preußischen Rheinprovinz, als Sohn eines Anwalts geboren; seine Geburtsurkunde stellte der Beigeordnete der Stadt, Emmerich Grach, aus – ein Vorfahr des Fernsehmoderators Günther Jauch, ein Detail, das regelmäßig in Quizsendungen auftaucht. Nach dem Studium in Bonn und Berlin und Jahren des Exils in Paris und Brüssel ließ sich Marx 1849 in London nieder und blieb dort bis an sein Lebensende; im Lesesaal des British Museum schrieb er „Das Kapital“. Er starb 1883 in London und liegt auf dem Highgate Cemetery.\n\n"],["=",299],["+","\n| Karl Marx | 1818, Trier | London | 1883 |"]]}]},
